    <bpmn:process id="W_W1177" name="W1177. Enterprise Data Governance Council, Standards &amp; Stewardship Program" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly Data Governance Council meeting; or data quality incident escalation; or new data domain onboarding (e.g., new ERP module go-live)
Frequency: Monthly Council meetings; weekly steward working sessions; continuous governance operations
Volume: 35,000 active SKUs, 200 stores, 5 legal entities, ~800 vendors, ~6,932 employees — all generating data across 30+ ERP modules
Owner: Data Governance Lead / CIO
Participants: Data Governance Council (CIO, CFO, COO, VP Merchandising, CHRO, Legal), Data Stewards (1 per functional domain), Data Architect, BI Manager
Source: workflow W1177 — Enterprise Data Governance Council, Standards &amp; Stewardship Program</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1177_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1177_Lane1" name="Data Governance Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1177_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1177_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1177_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1177_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1177_Lane2" name="Data Stewards">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1177_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1177_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1177_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1177_Lane4" name="Data Architect">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1177_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1177_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1177_Start6" name="Monthly Data Governance Council meeting; or data quality incident escalation; or new data…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1177_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1177_Task7" name="Data Governance Council meeting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Data Governance Council meeting (monthly): Council reviews: (a) data quality scorecard — key metrics by domain (customer data accuracy, product data completeness, financial data timeliness); (b) critical data incidents from past month; (c) remediation progress on open issues; (d) new data domain requests (e.g., ecommerce platform data integration per W706); (e) data privacy compliance update per W647; (f) policy changes for approval; (g) stewardship program progress
Responsible (R): Data Governance Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1177_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1177_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1177_Task8" name="Data domain stewardship">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Data domain stewardship (ongoing): Domain Data Stewards (1 each for: Product, Customer, Vendor, Finance, HR, Supply Chain, Store Operations) manage: (a) Product Steward: SKU data quality, attribute completeness, category hierarchy accuracy, pricing consistency across channels per W678; (b) Customer Steward: duplicate detection and merging, loyalty account integrity per W551, credit data accuracy per W783; (c) Vendor Steward: vendor master accuracy, bank account verification, compliance document currency per W870; (d) Finance Steward: GL account structure, cost center accuracy, intercompany elimination data per W87; (e) HR Steward: employee master accuracy, payroll data integrity, org hierarchy; (f) Supply Chain Steward: inventory accuracy across DC/store/ecom, ATP data reliability; (g) Store Ops Steward: store master data, POS configuration accuracy, facility data
Responsible (R): Data Stewards
Accountable (A): Data Governance Lead
Duration: 4–6 hours/week each</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1177_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1177_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1177_Task9" name="Data standards enforcement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Data standards enforcement: Data Governance Lead publishes and maintains standards: (a) naming conventions (customer name format: Last, First Middle; vendor legal name per SEC registration); (b) mandatory fields per entity (SKU: description, category, unit of measure, weight, dimensions, cost, price — all required); (c) data format standards (dates: YYYY-MM-DD; currency: PHP with 2 decimal places; phone: +63 format); (d) data entry validation rules enforced in ERP; (e) exception handling process for data that doesn&#x27;t fit standard formats
Responsible (R): Data Governance Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1177_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1177_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1177_Task10" name="Data quality monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Data quality monitoring: System monitors data quality across domains: (a) completeness: % of mandatory fields populated; (b) accuracy: % of records matching validation rules; (c) timeliness: % of records updated within SLA; (d) consistency: % of records matching across systems (e.g., customer record identical in POS, CRM, and ERP); (e) uniqueness: duplicate record detection; (f) quality score per domain published on governance dashboard; (g) domains scoring &lt; 90% trigger steward investigation
Responsible (R): System / Data Stewards
Accountable (A): Data Governance Lead
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1177_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1177_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1177_Task11" name="Data lineage &amp; catalog management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Data lineage &amp; catalog management: Data Architect maintains enterprise data catalog: (a) document all data entities, their source systems, transformation rules, and consumption points; (b) map data lineage: source → ETL → warehouse → dashboard/report; (c) identify data dependencies and impact of source changes; (d) publish data dictionary accessible to all BI users per W882 self-service governance; (e) update catalog when new modules, integrations, or reports are deployed
Responsible (R): Data Architect
Accountable (A): Data Governance Lead
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1177_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1177_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1177_Task12" name="Policy compliance audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Policy compliance audit: Quarterly, Data Governance Lead audits compliance with: (a) data retention policy (financial: 10 years per BIR; employee: per DOLE requirements; customer: per RA 10173 privacy law); (b) data access controls per W647 privacy compliance; (c) data sharing agreements with third parties (vendors per W705, delivery partners per W1163, payment gateways); (d) results reported to Council with remediation actions
Responsible (R): Data Governance Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1177_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1177_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1177_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1177_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1177_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-326 (ensure controlled execution — Data Engineering &amp; Quality (PA-28.2).)
Owner: Data Governance Lead / CIO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
