    <bpmn:process id="W_W1390" name="W1390. Store POS Transaction Data Quality Validation, Anomaly Detection &amp; Correction Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — daily (post-ETL validation); ad-hoc triggered by BI report discrepancy or analytics model error
Frequency: Daily automated validation; weekly manual anomaly review
Volume: ~2.8M POS transactions/month across 200 stores; daily validation of ~90,000–100,000 transactions
Owner: Data Quality Analyst
Participants: Data Quality Analyst, BI Manager, Store Operations (for corrections), IT (for system fixes)
Source: workflow W1390 — Store POS Transaction Data Quality Validation, Anomaly Detection &amp; Correction Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1390_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1390_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1390_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1390_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1390_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1390_Lane2" name="Data Quality Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1390_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1390_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1390_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1390_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1390_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1390_Start4" name="Scheduled — daily (post-ETL validation); ad-hoc triggered by BI report discrepancy or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1390_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1390_Task5" name="Automated daily validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Automated daily validation (post-ETL, 7:00 AM): data quality engine runs ~50 validation rules against previous day&#x27;s POS transactions: (a) Completeness: every transaction has store code, terminal ID, timestamp, cashier ID, total amount; every line item has SKU, quantity, unit price; (b) Validity: store code matches location master; SKU matches product master; payment method code is valid; (c) Consistency: transaction total = sum of line items; tax amount consistent with 12% VAT; discounts applied per approved promo codes; (d) Uniqueness: no duplicate transaction IDs across all stores; (e) Timeliness: all stores have submitted data within SLA (upload within 2 hours of store close); (f) Business rules: no negative revenue without corresponding return/refund transaction; no loyalty points earned on voided transactions; no employee purchases with irregular discount patterns
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1390_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1390_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1390_Task6" name="Anomaly detection engine">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Anomaly detection engine (daily): machine learning model flags statistical anomalies: (a) store daily revenue &gt; 3 standard deviations from rolling 30-day average; (b) transaction count per terminal &gt; 2× average for day-of-week; (c) unusual SKU mix (high-value items concentrated in single transactions); (d) excessive void rate per cashier (&gt; 10% of transactions); (e) average transaction value spikes &gt; 50% from 30-day average
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1390_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1390_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1390_Task7" name="Exception triage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Exception triage (8:00 AM): Data Quality Analyst reviews validation results and anomaly flags: (a) categorize exceptions by severity — Critical (affects financial reporting), High (affects operational reporting), Medium (affects analytics), Low (cosmetic); (b) Critical: investigate immediately before morning report distribution (W879); (c) High: investigate within 24 hours; (d) Medium/Low: queue for weekly batch review
Responsible (R): Data Quality Analyst
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 30–60 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1390_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1390_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1390_Task8" name="Root cause investigation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Root cause investigation: for each exception, Data Quality Analyst traces data lineage: (a) is the issue at source (POS entry error, hardware malfunction) or at ETL (data transformation error, mapping failure)? (b) is it isolated to one store or systemic? (c) is it a recurring pattern or one-time event?
Responsible (R): Data Quality Analyst
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 15–30 min/exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1390_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1390_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1390_Task9" name="Correction processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Correction processing: (a) Source correction: if POS data entry error, coordinate with Store Manager for transaction correction in POS system; correction flows through next ETL cycle; (b) Data warehouse correction: if ETL transformation error, Data Quality Analyst applies correction in staging layer with documented justification; corrected data refreshes downstream reports; (c) System fix: if root cause is POS software bug or ETL mapping error, submit IT ticket for system fix; track until resolved
Responsible (R): Data Quality Analyst / IT
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 15–60 min/correction</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1390_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1390_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1390_Task10" name="Weekly data quality scorecard">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Weekly data quality scorecard: Data Quality Analyst generates weekly scorecard: (a) overall data quality score (% of transactions passing all validation rules), (b) exception volume by category and severity, (c) mean time to resolution, (d) recurring issues by store or category, (e) trend vs. prior weeks; BI Manager reviews and escalates systemic issues to IT or Store Operations
Responsible (R): Data Quality Analyst
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1390_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1390_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1390_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1390_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1390_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-326 (ensure controlled execution — Data Engineering &amp; Quality (PA-28.2).) | - operational: every pipeline error corrected via documented change approval with before/after data-quality evidence and audit trail
Owner: Data Quality Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
