    <bpmn:process id="W_W1391" name="W1391. Master Data Duplicate Detection, Merge Processing &amp; Golden Record Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — weekly duplicate detection scan; ad-hoc triggered by customer complaint (multiple accounts), vendor payment confusion (duplicate vendor), or product data inconsistency (duplicate SKUs)
Frequency: Weekly automated scan; ~20–30 potential duplicates flagged per week across all master data domains
Volume: ~1,200–1,500 potential duplicates reviewed/year; ~800–1,000 confirmed merges/year
Owner: Data Steward (within Master Data Management team)
Participants: Data Steward, Data Governance Lead, Customer Service (for customer merges), Merchandising (for product merges), Procurement (for vendor merges)
Source: workflow W1391 — Master Data Duplicate Detection, Merge Processing &amp; Golden Record Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1391_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1391_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1391_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1391_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1391_Lane2" name="Data Steward">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1391_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1391_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1391_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1391_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1391_Lane3" name="Data Governance Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1391_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1391_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1391_Start5" name="Scheduled — weekly duplicate detection scan; ad-hoc triggered by customer complaint…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1391_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1391_Task6" name="Weekly duplicate detection scan">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly duplicate detection scan: system runs fuzzy-matching algorithms across each master data domain: (a) Customers: match on name + phone, name + email, name + address, TIN (for trade accounts); threshold: &gt; 85% similarity score flagged as potential duplicate; (b) Products: match on SKU description, vendor item code, barcode/EAN; threshold: &gt; 90% similarity; (c) Vendors: match on vendor name + TIN, vendor name + bank account; threshold: &gt; 85% similarity; (d) generate potential duplicate queue sorted by match confidence and business impact
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (weekly)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1391_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1391_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1391_Task7" name="Manual review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Manual review: Data Steward reviews each potential duplicate pair: (a) examine both records in detail — all fields, transaction history, related records (orders, invoices, payments); (b) confirm or reject duplicate status; (c) for ambiguous cases (e.g., two &quot;Juan Cruz&quot; records with similar addresses — could be father and son, or true duplicate), check supplementary sources (phone call to customer, trade reference check, SEC/DTI records for business accounts)
Responsible (R): Data Steward
Accountable (A): Data Governance Lead
Duration: 10–20 min/pair</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1391_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1391_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1391_Task8" name="Merge processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Merge processing (for confirmed duplicates): (a) Data Steward identifies the &quot;golden record&quot; (more complete data, longer history, active status); (b) system re-links all transactions, invoices, payments, and loyalty activity from the secondary record to the golden record; (c) secondary record status changed to &quot;Merged — Superseded by [golden record ID]&quot;; (d) system validates data integrity: all financial balances (AR, loyalty points) consolidated correctly; no orphaned transactions; (e) Data Steward approves merge after validation
Responsible (R): Data Steward
Accountable (A): Data Governance Lead
Duration: 15–30 min/merge</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1391_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1391_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1391_Task9" name="Domain-specific merge rules">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Domain-specific merge rules: (a) Customer merges: consolidate loyalty points (sum), AR balance (sum), purchase history (union); update CRM profile with most recent contact information; notify customer if address/phone changes; (b) Product merges: consolidate inventory quantities, sales history, and replenishment parameters; deprecate secondary SKU; update all open POs and transfer orders; update planogram assignments; (c) Vendor merges: consolidate spend history, open POs, and contract records; deprecate secondary vendor code; notify vendor of consolidated vendor code
Responsible (R): Data Steward / Domain Owner
Accountable (A): Data Governance Lead
Duration: 15–30 min/merge</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1391_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1391_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1391_Task10" name="Post-merge monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-merge monitoring: for 30 days after merge, Data Steward monitors for: (a) failed transactions referencing merged (superseded) record; (b) data integrity issues (duplicate re-creation by new entries); (c) user complaints about merged records; resolve any issues
Responsible (R): Data Steward
Accountable (A): Data Governance Lead
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1391_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1391_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1391_Task11" name="Monthly duplicate prevention review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly duplicate prevention review: Data Governance Lead reviews duplicate creation patterns — (a) which entry points generate the most duplicates? (POS enrollment, ecommerce registration, trade account applications); (b) implement preventive measures: real-time duplicate detection at entry, mandatory TIN validation for trade accounts, POS enrollment deduplication check (fuzzy match before creating new record); (c) measure duplicate rate trend month-over-month
Responsible (R): Data Governance Lead
Accountable (A): MDM Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1391_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1391_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1391_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1391_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1391_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-326 (ensure controlled execution — Data Engineering &amp; Quality (PA-28.2).) | - operational: performance
Owner: Data Steward (within Master Data Management team)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
