    <bpmn:process id="W_W1481" name="W1481. Data Pipeline Disaster Recovery, Failover Testing &amp; RTO/RPO Validation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly DR test schedule; or actual data pipeline failure (DC outage, cloud provider incident); or major system upgrade requiring DR validation
Frequency: Quarterly DR test; continuous monitoring; ad-hoc for actual incidents
Volume: ~50–80 ETL pipelines (per W881); ~20,000 job executions/month; ~1,000 GB data warehouse
Owner: Data Engineer
Participants: BI Manager, IT Database Administrator, IT Infrastructure, Cloud Provider, Data Quality Analyst
Source: workflow W1481 — Data Pipeline Disaster Recovery, Failover Testing &amp; RTO/RPO Validation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1481_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1481_Lane1" name="Data Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1481_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1481_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1481_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1481_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1481_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1481_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1481_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1481_Start3" name="Quarterly DR test schedule; or actual data pipeline failure (DC outage, cloud provider…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1481_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1481_Task4" name="DR architecture &amp; RTO/RPO definition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: DR architecture &amp; RTO/RPO definition: (a) Data Engineer documents current DR architecture: (i) cloud region and availability zone configuration, (ii) database replication strategy (synchronous vs. asynchronous), (iii) ETL pipeline redundancy, (iv) backup frequency and retention; (b) BI Manager defines RTO/RPO targets by data domain: (i) POS sales data: RPO &lt; 1 hour, RTO &lt; 4 hours (daily operations depend on this), (ii) Financial data: RPO &lt; 15 min, RTO &lt; 2 hours (month-end close critical), (iii) Inventory data: RPO &lt; 1 hour, RTO &lt; 4 hours (replenishment depends on this), (iv) HR/payroll data: RPO &lt; 1 hour, RTO &lt; 8 hours (semi-monthly payroll cycles), (v) Historical/analytics data: RPO &lt; 24 hours, RTO &lt; 24 hours (can tolerate longer recovery)
Responsible (R): Data Engineer / BI Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Initial: 2–3 days; maintenance: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1481_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1481_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1481_Task5" name="Quarterly DR test execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quarterly DR test execution: (a) Data Engineer schedules quarterly DR test (coordinated with IT Infrastructure per W26 BCP testing): (i) Tabletop exercise (Q1, Q3): walk-through of DR procedures with all stakeholders — simulate primary database failure, document step-by-step recovery process, identify gaps; (ii) Live failover test (Q2, Q4): execute actual failover to DR environment: redirect ETL pipelines to secondary database, verify data completeness, run critical reports against DR environment, measure actual RTO achieved, failback to primary; (b) Data Quality Analyst validates data in DR environment: (i) row counts match primary, (ii) most recent data available within RPO target, (iii) critical reports produce correct results
Responsible (R): Data Engineer / Data Quality Analyst
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1481_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1481_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1481_Task6" name="RTO/RPO validation &amp; gap analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: RTO/RPO validation &amp; gap analysis: (a) after each DR test: Data Engineer documents results: (i) actual RTO achieved vs. target, (ii) actual RPO achieved vs. target, (iii) any data loss during failover, (iv) any ETL pipelines that failed in DR environment, (v) any reports that produced incorrect results; (b) if RTO/RPO not met: root cause analysis and remediation plan — (i) is the architecture adequate? (need faster replication, additional resources?), (ii) is the procedure adequate? (manual steps too slow?), (iii) is the team trained? (confusion during failover?)
Responsible (R): Data Engineer
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 4 hours/test</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1481_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1481_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1481_Task7" name="Backup validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Backup validation: (a) monthly: Data Engineer verifies backup integrity: (i) automated backup completion check (all databases backed up per schedule), (ii) random backup restore test (restore one table from backup, verify data matches production), (iii) backup storage capacity check (1,000 GB growing at ~10–15% annually — is storage scaling?), (iv) backup encryption verification (data at rest encrypted per W647 privacy compliance); (b) backup retention validation: (i) 10-year retention for financial data per BIR requirements, (ii) 3-year retention for operational data, (iii) purge expired backups
Responsible (R): Data Engineer / IT DBA
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1481_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1481_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1481_Task8" name="Actual incident recovery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Actual incident recovery: When a real data pipeline failure occurs: (a) Data Engineer activates DR procedure: (i) assess failure scope (single pipeline, full database, cloud region), (ii) determine if failover to DR is required or if repair in primary is faster, (iii) execute recovery per documented procedure; (b) during recovery: communicate status to stakeholders (BI Manager → affected business users); (c) post-recovery: document incident, actual RTO achieved, root cause, and preventive measures — feed into next quarterly DR test
Responsible (R): Data Engineer / BI Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1481_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1481_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1481_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1481_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1481_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-326 (ensure controlled execution — Data Engineering &amp; Quality (PA-28.2).) | - operational: testing during low-activity hours (Sunday morning); operational: tabletop exercises (Q1, Q3) that keep procedures fresh without full failover risk
Owner: Data Engineer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1481_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1481_Annotation10" targetRef="W1481_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1481_Flow12" sourceRef="W1481_Start3" targetRef="W1481_Task4" />
