    <bpmn:process id="W_W1482" name="W1482. Master Data Change Impact Analysis, Propagation Tracking &amp; Downstream Notification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Proposed change to master data record (SKU, customer, vendor, GL account, store location); or emergency master data correction
Frequency: ~100–200 master data changes/month (price changes, vendor updates, store configuration changes, customer merges per W1391)
Volume: 35,000 active SKUs, ~5,400 trade/corporate customers, ~1,000 vendors, 205 locations, ~500–800 GL accounts per entity
Owner: Data Governance Lead
Participants: Data Steward, Data Engineer, Category Manager, Finance, IT, Store Operations
Source: workflow W1482 — Master Data Change Impact Analysis, Propagation Tracking &amp; Downstream Notification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1482_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1482_Lane1" name="Requestor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1482_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1482_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1482_Lane2" name="Data Steward">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1482_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1482_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1482_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1482_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1482_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1482_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1482_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1482_Start5" name="Proposed change to master data record (SKU, customer, vendor, GL account, store…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1482_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1482_Task6" name="Change request submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Change request submission: (a) requestor (Category Manager, Finance, Store Operations, etc.) submits master data change request in the Data Governance module: (i) what record needs to change (entity type + ID), (ii) current value → proposed new value, (iii) reason for change, (iv) urgency (standard = 5 business days, emergency = 24 hours); (b) system routes request to the appropriate Data Steward based on master data domain (Product, Customer, Vendor, Finance, HR, Supply Chain, Store Ops)
Responsible (R): Requestor / System
Accountable (A): Data Steward
Duration: 10 min/request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1482_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1482_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1482_Task7" name="Impact analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Impact analysis: (a) Data Steward performs automated impact analysis: (i) system identifies all downstream consumers of the affected record: ERP modules, POS, ecommerce, WMS, CRM, loyalty, marketplace integrations, BI reports, bank files, tax reports; (ii) system identifies all active transactions referencing the record: open POs, pending invoices, active orders, transfer orders; (iii) system estimates change propagation complexity: Low (simple field update, auto-propagated), Medium (requires downstream system configuration update), High (requires manual intervention in multiple systems); (b) Data Steward assesses risk: (i) what breaks if the change is executed incorrectly? (ii) what is the rollback plan? (iii) should the change be staged (execute in phases) or immediate?
Responsible (R): Data Steward / System
Accountable (A): Data Governance Lead
Duration: 15–30 min/change</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1482_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1482_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1482_Task8" name="Change approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Change approval: (a) for Low-complexity changes: Data Steward approves and executes; (b) for Medium-complexity changes: Data Governance Lead approves; (c) for High-complexity changes: approval from affected domain owners (e.g., GL change requires Controller approval, store configuration change requires COO approval); (d) for emergency changes: Data Steward executes immediately with verbal approval from Data Governance Lead, followed by written documentation within 24 hours
Responsible (R): Data Steward / Data Governance Lead
Accountable (A): Domain Owner (if High)
Duration: 5–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1482_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1482_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1482_Task9" name="Change execution &amp; propagation tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Change execution &amp; propagation tracking: (a) Data Steward executes the change in the master data record; (b) system automatically propagates the change to all identified downstream systems; (c) system tracks propagation status per downstream system: Pending → Propagated → Verified; (d) Data Engineer monitors propagation for completeness: (i) ecommerce catalog updated? (ii) POS price/product lookup updated? (iii) marketplace listings updated per W1464? (iv) BI reports reflecting new data? (v) AP vendor bank details updated?; (e) any propagation failures: Data Engineer troubleshoots and re-triggers
Responsible (R): Data Steward / Data Engineer / System
Accountable (A): Data Governance Lead
Duration: Variable</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1482_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1482_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1482_Task10" name="Downstream notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Downstream notification: (a) system auto-notifies affected stakeholders of the completed change: (i) product data changes → Category Manager, Ecommerce Manager, Content Manager; (ii) customer data changes → CSR, Sales, AR; (iii) vendor data changes → Procurement, AP; (iv) financial data changes → Controller, AR, AP, Treasury; (v) store configuration changes → Store Manager, Regional Ops Manager; (b) notification includes: what changed, old value → new value, effective date, any action required by the stakeholder
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Data Governance Lead
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1482_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1482_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1482_Task11" name="Post-change validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-change validation: (a) 24 hours after change: Data Steward validates downstream impact: (i) spot-check 3–5 downstream systems for correct data propagation, (ii) check customer/employee complaints related to the change, (iii) verify no downstream system errors in IT monitoring; (b) if issues detected: initiate remediation and update change procedure to prevent recurrence
Responsible (R): Data Steward
Accountable (A): Data Governance Lead
Duration: 15 min/change</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1482_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1482_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1482_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1482_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1482_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-326 (ensure controlled execution — Data Engineering &amp; Quality (PA-28.2).) | - operational: Data Governance Lead review and approval gate
Owner: Data Governance Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1482_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1482_Annotation13" targetRef="W1482_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
